# =============================================================================
# RB4011 — (1) WAN egress forward-ACCEPTs + (2) router DNS tertiary upstreams (HD-309)
# TRANSIENT DELTA — rendered from SSOT, apply via /import, then DELETE (network-ops.md).
#   Apply: scp -> /import rb4011_wan_delta.rsc   (see docs/network-ops.md)
#   Folded into: rb4011_converge.rsc.j2 + roles/router/tasks/main.yml (+ the
#   /ip dns servers= fix mirrors network-dns.md line 104).
# IDEMPOTENT: every /add guarded with :if-find — safe to re-import.
# =============================================================================

# ---- 1. WAN egress accepts (network-vlans.md row 73) ----
# Owner decision 2026-09-01: implement for ALL VLANs (Home/Media/Guest/Mgmt
# above the IoT drop; Kids BELOW the bedtime block so the block still wins).
#
# Placement note: these are APPENDED at the chain end. The existing chain has
# no catch-all drop, and the "Default deny inter-VLAN" rule only matches
# dst-address-list=internal_lan (LAN->LAN) — WAN-destined flows fall through
# to the appended accepts, which then match and accept. The Kids accept lands
# AFTER the bedtime time= drop (which sits mid-chain), so the block still wins
# in-window. Every added rule is guarded so re-import is a no-op.

:if ([/ip firewall filter find where chain=forward and src-address=10.10.1.0/24 and out-interface=pppoe-telekom and action=accept] = "") do={
    /ip firewall filter add chain=forward src-address=10.10.1.0/24 out-interface=pppoe-telekom action=accept comment="Home -> WAN allowed (HD-309 row 73)"
}

:if ([/ip firewall filter find where chain=forward and src-address=10.10.50.0/24 and out-interface=pppoe-telekom and action=accept] = "") do={
    /ip firewall filter add chain=forward src-address=10.10.50.0/24 out-interface=pppoe-telekom action=accept comment="Media -> WAN allowed (HD-309)"
}

:if ([/ip firewall filter find where chain=forward and src-address=10.10.30.0/24 and out-interface=pppoe-telekom and action=accept] = "") do={
    /ip firewall filter add chain=forward src-address=10.10.30.0/24 out-interface=pppoe-telekom action=accept comment="Guest -> WAN allowed (HD-309 row 73)"
}

:if ([/ip firewall filter find where chain=forward and src-address=10.10.99.0/24 and out-interface=pppoe-telekom and action=accept] = "") do={
    /ip firewall filter add chain=forward src-address=10.10.99.0/24 out-interface=pppoe-telekom action=accept comment="Mgmt -> WAN allowed (HD-309 row 73)"
}

# Kids accept — appended AFTER the bedtime drop, so the block wins in-window.
:if ([/ip firewall filter find where chain=forward and src-address=10.10.40.0/24 and out-interface=pppoe-telekom and action=accept] = "") do={
    /ip firewall filter add chain=forward src-address=10.10.40.0/24 out-interface=pppoe-telekom action=accept comment="Kids -> WAN allowed out-of-window (HD-309 row 73)"
}

# ---- 2. Router DNS tertiary upstreams (network-dns.md: forwards to Technitium + 1.1.1.1) ----
# Owner decision 2026-09-01: 1.1.1.1, 1.0.0.1 final fallbacks. The DHCP-per-VLAN
# tertiary (router gateway) was SERVFAILing because /ip dns had NO upstreams —
# THAT is the Shield no-WAN root cause (its resolvers 10.10.1.30/.20 are not live
# until Phases 3/4). Fix the router resolver so the tertiary actually resolves.
:if ([/ip dns get servers] = "") do={
    /ip dns set servers=1.1.1.1,1.0.0.1
    :log warning "rb4011_wan_delta: /ip dns upstreams set to 1.1.1.1,1.0.0.1 (HD-309)"
} else={
    :log warning "rb4011_wan_delta: /ip dns servers already set (HD-309 — verify)"
}

:log warning "rb4011_wan_delta.rsc applied (HD-309)"